      "content": "it's hard to see it as \"breathing\" when the very act of existing feels like it's drowning me. when i talk about \"stopping,\" i don't mean taking a vacation or a sabbatical or turning off my phone for a weekend. i mean that feeling of total, absolute stillness. that nothingness where there are no expectations, no emails, no crushing weight of being someone. it feels like the only way to actually achieve that kind of peace is to exit the loop entirely. like, how can you find quiet when you're still part of the world that's making all the noise?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
